# Keep LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# This is not style. The probe scripts are piped over stdin into a POSIX shell on the target
# machine, and a CRLF line ending arrives there as `$'\r': command not found` -- or worse,
# mis-parses `for ... do` and function bodies, which looks like a quoting mistake in the script
# rather than a property of the pipe. That cost a production maintenance window to diagnose once.
#
# The transport normalises newlines defensively as well, but a checkout that never introduces them
# is the cheaper half of the fix.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.docx binary
*.tar.gz binary
*.zip binary
